-- Fraud Act 2006 (2006 c. 35): THE SHAPE SHARED BY THE PENALTY SUBSECTIONS.
--
-- Sections 1(3), 6(2), 7(2), 9(6) and 11(3) say the same thing in the same words, except for the
-- number of years on indictment (10, 5, 10, 10, 5).  Sections 1(4), 6(3), 7(3), 9(7) and 11(4)
-- say the same Northern Ireland thing five times.  Paragraph 1 of Schedule 2 says the same
-- thing about offences committed before 2 May 2022 for all five.  This module states each of
-- those rules ONCE; the module of each section states its own number of years and calls the
-- shape.  Penalties are taken from the text only: nothing is imported from sentencing law.
--
-- A penalty is a CEILING, never a sentence: the court may impose less.  Where the Act gives no
-- figure ("the general limit in a magistrates' court", "the statutory maximum", "a fine") the
-- result says so in words and carries no number.

§ `Penalties: the shape shared by sections 1, 6, 7, 9 and 11`

§§ `Northern Ireland and offences before 2 May 2022 (sections 1(4), 6(3), 7(3), 9(7), 11(4); Schedule 2 paragraph 1)`

-- src:16 | (4) Subsection (3)(a) applies in relation to Northern Ireland as if the reference to 12 months were a reference to 6 months.
-- src:58 | (3) Subsection (2)(a) applies in relation to Northern Ireland as if the reference to 12 months were a reference to 6 months.
-- src:66 | (3) Subsection (2)(a) applies in relation to Northern Ireland as if the reference to 12 months were a reference to 6 months.
-- src:91 | (7) Subsection (6)(a) applies in relation to Northern Ireland as if the reference to 12 months were a reference to 6 months.
-- src:109 | (4) Subsection (3)(a) applies in relation to Northern Ireland as if the reference to 12 months were a reference to 6 months.
@ref Fraud Act 2006 ss 1(4), 6(3), 7(3), 9(7), 11(4) (src:16) (src:58) (src:66) (src:91) (src:109)
GIVEN place IS A Place
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sections 1(4), 6(3), 7(3), 9(7) and 11(4): in Northern Ireland the limit on summary conviction is read as 6 months` place MEANS
    -- Reading taken (fork F2 in NOTES.md): the text says "as if the reference to 12 months were a
    -- reference to 6 months", but the subsections it modifies no longer contain "12 months"; they say
    -- "the general limit in a magistrates' court".  The evident effect, six months, is taken.
    place EQUALS `Northern Ireland`

-- src:343 | Maximum term of imprisonment for offences under this Act
-- src:344 | 1 In relation to an offence committed before 2 May 2022, the references to the general limit in a magistrates’ court in sections 1(3)(a), 6(2)(a), 7(2)(a), 9(6)(a) and 11(3)(a) are to be read as references to 6 months.
@ref Fraud Act 2006 Schedule 2 paragraph 1 (src:344)
GIVEN `the date the offence was committed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule 2 paragraph 1: the offence was committed before 2 May 2022` `the date the offence was committed` MEANS
    -- "Before" is strict: an offence committed ON 2 May 2022 is not committed before it.
    `the date the offence was committed` LESS THAN `Schedule 2 paragraph 1: the date from which the general limit is not read as 6 months`

