@ref Fraud Act 2006 ss 1(3)(a), 6(2)(a), 7(2)(a), 9(6)(a), 11(3)(a) with s 1(4) and Schedule 2 paragraph 1 (src:14) (src:56) (src:64) (src:89) (src:107)
GIVEN place IS A Place
      `the date the offence was committed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Summary imprisonment limit`
`sections 1(3)(a), 6(2)(a), 7(2)(a), 9(6)(a) and 11(3)(a): the longest term on summary conviction` place `the date the offence was committed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `sections 1(4), 6(3), 7(3), 9(7) and 11(4): in Northern Ireland the limit on summary conviction is read as 6 months` place
        THEN `six months`
        IF `Schedule 2 paragraph 1: the offence was committed before 2 May 2022` `the date the offence was committed`
        THEN `six months`
        OTHERWISE `the general limit in a magistrates' court (the Act states no figure)`

§§ `The penalty subsection, once (sections 1(3), 6(2), 7(2), 9(6), 11(3))`

-- src:13 | (3) A person who is guilty of fraud is liable—
-- src:14 | (a) on summary conviction, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding the general limit in a magistrates’ court or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or to both);
-- src:15 | (b) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 10 years or to a fine (or to both).
-- src:55 | (2) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:56 | (a) on summary conviction, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding the general limit in a magistrates’ court or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or to both);
-- src:57 | (b) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 5 years or to a fine (or to both).
-- src:63 | (2) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:64 | (a) on summary conviction, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding the general limit in a magistrates’ court or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or to both);
-- src:65 | (b) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 10 years or to a fine (or to both).
-- src:88 | (6) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:89 | (a) on summary conviction, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding the general limit in a magistrates’ court or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or to both);
-- src:90 | (b) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 10 years or to a fine (or to both).
-- src:106 | (3) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
